  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a **binary** string SSS of length NNN.\n\nYou can apply the following operation any (possibly zero) number of times:\n\n\nSelect an integer i&nbsp;(1≤i≤N−2)i\\ \\lparen 1 \\leq i \\leq N-2 \\rpareni&nbsp;(1≤i≤N−2) and replace the substring SiSi+1Si+2S_i S_{i+1} S_{i+2}Si​Si+1​Si+2​ with `100`.\nFind the **lexicographically smallest** string after the operations.\n\nNote: String XXX is lexicographically smaller than string YYY if Xi&lt;YiX_i \\lt Y_iXi​&lt;Yi​, where iii is the first index where XXX and YYY differ.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains an integer NNN — the length of string SSS.\nThe second line of each test case contains a binary string SSS.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the **lexicographically smallest** string after the operations.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "3≤N≤3⋅1053 \\leq N \\leq 3 \\cdot 10^53≤N≤3⋅105",
      "∣S∣=N|S| = N∣S∣=N",
      "Each character of SSS is either `0` or `1`.",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 3⋅1053 \\cdot 10^53⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n3\n110\n4\n0001",
        "output": "100\n0001",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: You can convert SSS into 100.\nSince 100 is lexicographically smaller than 110, output 100.\nTest case 222: You should keep SSS as it is without applying any operations, so output 0001."
      }
    ]
  },
